id: 1
event: turn_created
data: {"seq":1,"turn_id":"task_874dd3532420c1537b4a93379c9f3b0b","type":"turn_created","ts":"2026-11-26T18:30:57.105224+08:00","data":{"deep_research":false,"text":"# Cursor pagination skips tied timestamps\n\nRows have integer `time` and string `id` fields. The cursor is the last seen\n`[time, id]` pair. Fix `next_page` in `records.py` so pages preserve ascending\n`(time, id)` order and neither skip nor repeat a row when timestamps tie.\n\nThe contents of repo/ are already staged at the workspace root. The tool path for the target is exactly records.py. Use read_file on records.py first, write your change to records.py, then run a public smoke test with exec_shell.","turn_index":0},"internal":{"source":"host","type":"task_created","task_seq":1,"payload":{"text":"# Cursor pagination skips tied timestamps\n\nRows have integer `time` and string `id` fields. The cursor is the last seen\n`[time, id]` pair. Fix `next_page` in `records.py` so pages preserve ascending\n`(time, id)` order and neither skip nor repeat a row when timestamps tie.\n\nThe contents of repo/ are already staged at the workspace root. The tool path for the target is exactly records.py. Use read_file on records.py first, write your change to records.py, then run a public smoke test with exec_shell.","turn_index":0,"deep_research":false}}}

